\chapter{Filters and Operations}\label{ch:filters}

Filters keep the size of an image and change its content. LineScope offers the handful that people
most often want to compare: blurs, a median, sharpening, noise reduction, edge detectors, and two
per-pixel color maps. Where Core Image already has a good, well-known implementation it is used;
where a filter is simple enough to state in a few lines (the $3\times3$ kernels), it is written out, so
the reader can see precisely what was computed.

The second half of the chapter introduces [[ImageOperation]], the value that describes \emph{one
step} from one image to the next, whether that step is a filter or a resampling.

\section{The filters}

<<Packages/LineScopeCore/Sources/LineScopeCore/Filters.swift>>=
